WEBVTT

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:03.510
Stop that, Birdy, it's dangerous!

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.380
I'll be fine!

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.210
See, look!

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.820
Are you okay, Birdy?

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.810
Ow, ow, ow...

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:20.460
Sheesh, you're supposed to
be an lxioran? You're so clumsy.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.170
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:32.370
<i>Then we repeat, going</i>
<i>eternally round and round</i>

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:39.910
<i>Where will our path lead?</i>

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:46.420
<i>What do I lose sight of when I'm with you?</i>

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:54.090
<i>A colorful array of love and kindness</i>

00:00:54.090 --> 00:01:00.830
<i>I've remembered what</i>
<i>I'd forgotten since the days</i>

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:07.070
<i>when we hurt each other over trivial things</i>

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:14.380
<i>The sounds of our footsteps are</i>
<i>the "tracks" that lead to the future</i>

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:22.090
<i>Within the ever-changing scenery... always</i>

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:24.120
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:29.230
<i>Then we repeat, going</i>
<i>eternally round and round</i>

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:36.270
<i>This melody that paints the future,</i>
<i>until the world changes</i>

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:38.270
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:43.540
<i>The sun always rises again,</i>
<i>eternally repeating its arc</i>

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:54.390
<i>It lights up our path</i>

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.270
Atola satellite prison grants
permission for Tadmias to enter port.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.440
Guide rails in place. Course clear.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.430
We'll move the prisoners to the hatch gate.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.150
This is deceitful.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:25.180
A primitive planet or two is insignificant

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:29.760
if we can gain control of the Ryunka.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.350
The Sanctum Sanctorum knows that, so why...

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:38.100
Hey, that's the gate to the bridge!

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.690
Hey!

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:52.210
Huh?

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:53.840
What's wrong?

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:55.970
What's going on?

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:17.900
"One Month After the Strange Light"

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.540
It's been exactly one month since
the incident of the "strange light"

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:24.310
that resulted in unprecedented
casualties on the coast of Tokyo.

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:26.880
An international joint investigative team

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.150
is still working at the disaster site,

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.380
but they have not yet identified the cause.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:35.250
We also don't have a final number
on how many people are missing.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:37.890
This is Roppongi, which
received a direct hit from the light.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.490
Even the once-bustling shopping area

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:43.760
is now nothing but the endless
ruins you see behind me.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.700
The area is still sealed off out
of fear of secondary disasters,

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:49.170
and the public are not allowed in.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:52.840
The government's reconstruction
plans are not yet decided.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:57.670
And so you see our
great senior Sanada's report!

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:03.080
This incident resulted in so many casualties.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:07.550
We must do whatever we can now to help!

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:08.950
Therefore...!

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.410
"Our Theme for the 55th
Annual Culture Festival!!"
"We'll Investigate
the Lives of the Refugees!!"

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:16.230
Hey, are you guys actually listening to me?!

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.900
Dude, we're not <i>in</i> the Journalism Club.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:21.870
Yeah, why should we...

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:26.070
Wait, don't tell me you and Kitamura
are the only ones in your club?!

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:29.210
The upperclassmen retired in September.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:32.240
So I got dragged in on an emergency basis.

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:36.120
So specifically, do you
want to collect the views

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:38.120
of people on the street and report on that?

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.720
Yes, on the people in trouble, like
the ones still without basic utilities...

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:44.990
Wouldn't it be way better to
infiltrate the Roppongi ruins?

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:48.830
Yeah, that would link this
to our Ruins Exploration Club.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:52.900
Oh, and did you know about
the rumors that aliens did this?!

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:57.800
Yeah, and like, they're living all
over the place disguised as humans!

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.240
Seriously?!

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:03.080
A lot of people died, you guys!

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.070
Should you really be so
sensationalistic about this?!

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:14.150
That's my favorite pupil for you!
You say some smart things!

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:14.920
Who's that?

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:16.920
Oh, right, you haven't met him.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.120
What brings you here today, Muroto?

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.520
Well, you see...

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:22.700
"Do You Still Say Aliens Don't Exist?"
"by Keisuke Muroto"

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.760
Signed copies of my new book...

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:28.170
...for 1000 yen, a special
discount from 1500 yen

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:30.200
I'll take one!

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.270
Thanks!

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.940
A living example of sensationalism.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:35.870
It's basically just a festival.

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.540
We open up the school and have a good time.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:43.540
So Hayamiya's preparing a..."Sideshow"?
Yeah, I guess so.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.790
Who are you calling a festival sideshow?!

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:50.790
Oh, never mind, I was just talking to myself...

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.780
How dare you say that just
loud enough for me to hear?!

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:04.370
I told you I'm sorry. Stop being mad already.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:06.070
Don't talk to me.

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:09.310
I don't want people thinking
I know a space case like you.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:12.180
Don't call me a space case!

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:16.170
So you're obsessing over Nakasugi, then.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:28.030
I'm sorry! I crossed the line.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:30.660
Get it together, Senkawa!

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:35.330
Say... Do I have to help
you with the Culture Festival?

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:38.200
What, you don't want to
help out with some "sideshow"?

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:44.710
That's not it. I just... sort
of can't get into it, I guess...

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:50.880
Well, tough luck. You wounded my
maidenly heart saying that to me.

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:54.290
Whatever anyone else does,
<i>you</i> are going to help me!

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:55.190
What?!

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:56.960
So, that's settled.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:58.690
Hey!

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:00.090
Bye-bye!

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:02.760
Sheesh...

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:05.760
Why not just help her?

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:12.760
Well, but weren't we sort of
party to messing up Tokyo?

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:16.380
But...

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:20.970
It kind of feels like I'm being
told "This is what <i>you</i> did."

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:28.150
Hey Tsutomu, how are you? I bet
you're not dividing the garbage right!

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:32.720
That's not true. We did everything we could.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:38.300
If not for us, forget about Tokyo,
<i>all</i> humans would've been wiped out.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:39.920
Maybe so, but...

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:52.110
I think this feels more comfortable lately!

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:54.610
In other words, if we'd done a little more,

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:57.950
maybe we wouldn't be joined
again and we'd be better off...

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:01.790
Well, that happened
because you took in the Ryunka

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:04.620
to save Sayaka Nakasugi.

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:15.100
Plus, your body was so damaged it
was barely regenerable, you know.

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:18.000
It's sheer good luck that you're even alive.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.610
I know that in my head, but...

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:22.010
But...

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:26.610
Birdy, this is Megius.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.550
Birdy, where are you?

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:31.540
Here!

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:41.060
Are you familiar with the
Atola satellite prison, Birdy?

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:45.130
It's a life-sentence penal colony
where serious criminals are sent.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:48.300
The terrorist Kinzel Hower was confined there.

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:52.500
A convoy ship headed there was
hijacked by a group of prisoners.

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:54.840
A prison convoy ship?

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:59.830
Here's the data on the prisoners
and their suspected accessories.

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:06.390
Shi Rianshel, a former pontiff.

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:11.260
Agrazume Tula, a former
high-level Federation congressman.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:14.760
Faroid Kust...

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:18.060
...and his twin sister Tasera Kust.

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:22.500
They were head researchers at
a biochemical plant on Romekius.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:26.710
Gatol Bolan was a tactical commander
for the army's intelligence division.

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:32.040
His former subordinate, Moss Kiri,
was probably the insider on this escape.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.880
And then there's...

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:38.020
This Altan, Valic Nigua.

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:40.590
He's apparently a secret agent
for an antigovernment organization,

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:45.920
and he seems to have been involved
in this right from start to finish.

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:49.230
This is quite a lineup of prisoners...

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:51.260
What was their crime?

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:53.870
The Ryunka.

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:57.300
They're the ones who stole the
Ryunka from a government facility,

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:59.710
used Geega to transport it to Earth,

00:09:59.710 --> 00:10:02.910
and then attempted to test its power.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.580
They've infiltrated Earth.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:10.150
Birdy Cephon, your mission
is to capture them all unharmed

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:14.140
and return them to
Federation police headquarters.

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:18.590
They tried to turn Earth into a
guinea pig for their Ryunka experiments...

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:19.420
Does it bother you?

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:20.930
Of course it does!

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:24.260
Lots of people died because of them!

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:26.250
And Nakasugi...

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:33.970
I won't...

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:35.410
...ever forgive them.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:48.610
"Shion Arita"

00:10:57.030 --> 00:10:59.360
Bang!

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:03.700
Your heart is under arrest, yessiree!

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:05.500
Tee-hee!

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:07.440
Okay, cut!

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:10.010
That's a go, Shion baby!

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:12.140
Thank you, Sir!

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:13.280
Good work today.

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:14.680
Thanks, Ma'am!

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:21.990
Wow, that was good! Bravo! Shion is delicious!

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:24.560
Thank you, Mr. Ochikoshi.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:28.530
Her charm is definitely her uncontrived purity.

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:29.660
You flatter us.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:31.660
Though it's totally contrived.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:32.830
Leave me alone.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.200
Later.

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:36.740
Have a good day, Ma'am.

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:39.470
Tokyo's so down lately, you know?

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:43.740
So let's use Shion to fire everyone up!

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:47.150
I know, a unit! We'll get two
variety show girls and make a unit!
Um, Ma'am, may I talk to you for a moment?

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:48.180
I know, a unit! We'll get two
variety show girls and make a unit!
What?

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:49.880
I know, a unit! We'll get two
variety show girls and make a unit!
I don't have time for this stuff!
I have a new job and...

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:52.520
"Ali Baba"! We'll call it "Ali Baba!"
I don't have time for this stuff!
I have a new job and...

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:52.810
I don't have time for this stuff!
I have a new job and...

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:55.920
This is your job, too.

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:57.860
That's not what I mean; I
have to find the escapees...

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:01.160
Six months of advance
rent for your apartment.

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:03.160
And you want info too, right?

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:05.760
Well, that's true, but...

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:09.500
Then work... as Shion Arita.

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:12.400
You don't take Shion Arita,

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:15.170
the Earth persona <i>I
gave you, seriously enough.</i>

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.580
You get me, Ms. Irma? A dome!

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:20.250
Yes, yes, whatever you like.

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:22.080
Shion is the best!

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:27.570
"Shinmyou Books"

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:37.590
Dusk.

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:45.900
It's been a long time. Maybe fifteen years?

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:47.300
Fourteen.

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:10.760
What a filthy, filthy place!
Altans everywhere you look!

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:13.170
Your Excellency Rianshel, while it's true...

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:15.800
- that they look exactly like Altans...

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:17.600
- they're actually natives of this planet.

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:18.900
It's the same thing!

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:22.840
I cannot stand to hide on
such a disgusting planet!

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:25.240
True, it is ironic.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:28.080
Once we used this planet as a
testing ground for the Ryunka,

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:33.680
and now we have to disguise
ourselves as natives and lie low here...

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:40.960
It's done.

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:44.430
Wear it.

00:13:44.430 --> 00:13:46.670
How dare trash like you tell me...

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:49.800
While you're here, follow my orders.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:51.200
Hurry up.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.470
Why should I have to...

00:13:58.480 --> 00:13:59.950
What is this?

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:01.710
A mimesis chip.

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:03.820
Here on this hick planet?

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.620
Wh-What is this?

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:08.720
Your name is Lino Molelu.

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:10.960
You're a foreigner living in a hotel.

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:14.890
I never thought I'd have to
become an unsightly Altan...

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:16.360
It could be interesting.

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:17.130
Moss?

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:21.530
Colonel, it might be good to
try out being a gutless beast.

00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:37.050
An Altan...

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:38.580
- child.

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:39.920
Take these.

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:43.220
And this, too.

00:14:43.220 --> 00:14:45.260
A military woman should know what it is.

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:46.390
A communication device...

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:49.260
They're made the same
way as the old Radia ones.

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:50.900
You can use them to contact each other.

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:54.500
Contact me that way from now on, too.

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:57.400
This is disagreeable... truly disagreeable!

00:14:57.400 --> 00:14:58.870
Your Excellency Rianshel...

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:02.210
It's for your own sakes.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:06.910
While you're here, you can
buy time to cover up your crime.

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:09.110
Moss, you're behind this?

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:11.380
Our comrades within the government

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:14.950
will prove the rightness
of your actions without fail.

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:20.030
Hiding out as Altans?
You come up with some scary ideas.

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:23.190
My, but you look good,
Representative Agrazume.

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:24.030
How dare you!

00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:26.100
I'll say just one thing.

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:30.070
Become Earthlings. You'll lessen the danger

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:33.370
if you avoid attracting attention
and blend in with the Earthlings.

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:37.280
But if you should die, those chips
will disintegrate your bodies

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:39.880
and erase all evidence.

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:43.870
You see, I don't want the
Earthlings to find out about us.

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:49.920
Not that I think natives of
this planet could kill us...

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:53.290
There's one thing here that goes
beyond your expectations, Colonel.

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:54.730
What do you mean, Valic?

00:15:54.730 --> 00:15:59.100
That investigator who
sealed the Ryunka is still here.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:01.570
Birdy the Berserker Killer?!

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:06.300
That lxioran Altan, eh?
But she's no match for us on her own.

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:10.510
Well, just to be on the safe side,
behave yourselves and act as Altans...

00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:14.140
...no, as <i>Earthlings</i> for a while.

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:21.920
Dusk, it looks like you feel right
at home as an "escape man" now.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:25.820
You, the man once called
the Blue Fang of Isdalta...

00:16:25.820 --> 00:16:26.830
Whoa, there...

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:31.500
And it looks like your villainy
is deeply ingrained now, Valic.

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:33.470
I'm not a kid anymore, you see.

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:37.840
I've learned how to
get along in life, that's all.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:41.470
Come to think of it, is that reject still alive?

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:46.680
What's with you? It's early in the morning.

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:48.850
I'm still tired...

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:50.620
Hey, are you listening?

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:54.550
I can't let it go on this way!
I'm breaking things off with that hag!

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:56.050
Birdy?

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:58.990
At this rate, it'll interfere with my mission!

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:02.060
Oh, Shion Arita?

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:04.530
Running away?

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:06.800
Generally one does that at <i>night.</i>

00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:08.630
Um, er, I...

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:13.710
Are you sure about this?
I won't give you info or an allowance.

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:18.040
You won't be able to eat
your beloved rice balls anymore...

00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:21.480
Yeah, my allowance isn't
enough to cover everything <i>you</i> eat.

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:26.050
l-I have food on my spaceship...

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:29.050
But it's not tasty like rice is!

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:30.040
For goodness' sake...

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:36.530
This man who checked in to a
Shinjuku hotel a few days ago is suspicious.

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:37.660
Really?

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:40.870
Never underestimate the Altan Network.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:43.700
The man's name is Lino Molelu.

00:17:45.570 --> 00:17:49.440
He's in Room 2105 of the East Hotel.

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:53.040
He's supposed to be a French art dealer,

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:54.880
but he's no Earthling.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.280
Wh-Who are you?!

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:35.120
You're...

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:42.730
Here it is.

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:46.330
Hey Birdy, let's not do anything
to attract too much attention, okay?

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:48.900
Yeah, yeah.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:51.500
Aw, I knew it...

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:53.440
Excuse me!

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:54.840
Huh?

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:00.680
Lino Molelu.

00:19:00.680 --> 00:19:04.320
How cruel...

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:07.020
Hang in there!

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:09.690
Murderer! Murderer!

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:14.490
Somebody saw us, Birdy!

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:16.120
Rianshel?

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:20.960
He's melting...

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:30.640
In here! Room 2105!

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:32.630
- This is bad.
- Don't get close, not until the cops get here!

00:19:36.010 --> 00:19:37.450
Switch with me, Birdy.

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:38.850
Got it.

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:42.990
Ouch...

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:52.730
W-We hit somebody, Boss!

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:55.360
Wh-Why me?!

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:03.340
You say you slept through the whole night?

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:04.210
Yes...

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:06.340
Were you really hit by a car?

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:07.850
I think so...

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:10.420
The car's all beaten up!

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:12.680
Please check him out good, Doc!

00:20:12.680 --> 00:20:17.090
Gentlemen, he hasn't got a
scratch on him. His brain's fine, too.

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:18.820
S-So, Doc...

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:21.060
Does... Does that mean
the kid's gonna make it?!

00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:23.390
Yep, I don't think there's
anything to worry about.

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:25.560
Thank goodness!

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:28.330
Tsutomu, we shouldn't stick around too long.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:30.270
Well then, I'll just be going...

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:33.100
Come on back if you have
any symptoms of whiplash.

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:34.210
Yes, Doctor!

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:38.540
Hey, kid, come back!
If I let you go home now...

00:20:38.540 --> 00:20:41.350
Huh? He's gone.

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:43.080
What now?

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:45.350
I never imagined one of
the escapees would be killed...

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:46.940
But we still have a clue.

00:20:49.690 --> 00:20:51.560
That pendant-type thing?

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:53.750
Right. If we investigate that...

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:07.790
Are you all right?

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:13.480
Ouch!

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:14.410
Birdy.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:16.250
Huh?

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:20.240
You're as clumsy as ever.
And you're supposed to be an lxioran?

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:26.560
Nataru?

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:39.600
Nataru...

00:21:41.310 --> 00:21:46.140
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:21:46.140 --> 00:21:52.340
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:22:03.930 --> 00:22:09.430
<i>If you hang your head like that,</i>
<i>you won't get any sunlight</i>

00:22:09.430 --> 00:22:14.970
<i>Look up at the blue sky so you'll grow taller!</i>

00:22:14.970 --> 00:22:20.650
<i>Let's pour a few tears from the watering can</i>

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:26.640
<i>Eventually shoots will spring up</i>
<i>from somewhere in your heart</i>

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:32.360
<i>Let's take life slowly</i>

00:22:32.360 --> 00:22:37.360
<i>A girl's dreams are neverending</i>

00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:43.570
<i>Ah, there's someone</i>
<i>out there waiting for you</i>

00:22:43.570 --> 00:22:48.410
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:22:48.410 --> 00:22:55.080
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:59.880
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:22:59.880 --> 00:23:05.880
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:23:11.560 --> 00:23:15.400
<i>Hi, this is Birdy Cephon Altira!</i>

00:23:15.400 --> 00:23:20.200
<i>Looks like the adult me is an</i>
<i>investigator as planned. I'm glad!</i>

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:24.010
<i>And just think... I got to see Nataru again too!</i>

00:23:24.010 --> 00:23:27.380
<i>He's turned out pretty handsome!</i>

00:23:27.380 --> 00:23:32.780
<i>But it looks like we're mixed up in</i>
<i>some weird incidents, so I'm worried...</i>

00:23:32.780 --> 00:23:35.450
<i>Hang in there, future me!</i>

00:23:35.450 --> 00:23:38.450
<i>Violin, is the food ready yet?</i>
